title ALES35 — Lotus's rack merge: two saved racks joined, sealed import
prompt Continue the ALES recursion loop Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think ALES34's road-on named the next rungs: sign the seal (Kumara key — a module seam, gate #4) or carry a slot over the ALES0 wire (a network seam). Both wait for Keaton's word, so I took the keep-going alternative it also named: the next purely-local ergonomic rung on the sheet side.
think Chose it Lindy-first crux-first. Save (ALES33) · seal (ALES34) · load are incomplete while a loaded rack stands alone — a real session gathers stems from many places, so the missing gesture is MERGE: join a saved rack's named slots into the one already open. The load/import gesture is used ten thousand times over a DAW's life (Lindy); its hard-but-tractable core is atomicity across two racks (crux) — all-or-nothing on a collision or ceiling overflow, never touching a live slot's audio.
think Made atomicity exact with a precheck-before-any-write: decide RackFull (union past max_slots) and Duplicate (any src name already in dst) first, so the grafting copies are unconditional and a plain value-struct copy cannot fail — all-or-nothing without a scratch rack. Reused ALES30's disjoint Slot: dst.slots[dst.count] = src.slots[i] copies the whole embedded clipboard into dst's own storage, depending on no src memory. Self-merge collides on the first name and refuses Duplicate cleanly.
think Paid the ALES34 seal forward: verify_and_import composes verify_and_parse (integrity gate) into a temp rack, then merge — so a keeper loads a VERIFIED archive's stems into a live session in one call, and a tampered sheet refuses DigestMismatch before a single slot joins. The seal and the merge fit together as one durable gesture.
obs GREEN on the first build across six cases: a two-slot src merges whole into a two-slot dst (all four names in fill order, each channel byte-for-byte, src unchanged); a grafted slot survives a drop from src (disjoint); a name collision refuses Duplicate with dst untouched and no non-colliding slot leaking in; a union past the ceiling refuses RackFull, dst untouched; an empty src is a no-op; verify_and_import loads a sealed sheet into a live rack and a tampered sheet refuses DigestMismatch before a slot joins.
obs Witness tools/ales_rack_merge_witness.rish GREEN; tame_style_check GREEN (bans clean, no new zero-assert file, no usize, no bare memcpy); RackMergeError = rack.RackError (no new fault), RackImportError = rack_seal.RackSealError || rack.RackError. Purely local — grafting fixed-array value structs in process; no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real meter, no real speaker; every custody gate untouched.
loom witness=ales_rack_merge_witness result=green build=first cases=6 new_fault=0 reused=rack_slot+verify_and_parse
file lotus/rack_merge.rye ALES35 module — merge (atomic disjoint graft of two racks) and verify_and_import (sealed load into a live rack)
file tools/ales_rack_merge_witness.rish the witness that builds and proves it GREEN on metal
